 apparatus. A method of external splinting of the cervical spine after injury</article-title><source>J Bone Joint Surg Br</source><year>1962</year><volume>44-B</volume><fpage>655</fpage><lpage>661</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14039708</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ryan</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>TK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Odontoid fractures. A rational approach to treatment</article-title><source>J Bone Joint Surg Br</source><year>1982</year><volume>64</volume><fpage>416</fpage><lpage>421</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7096414</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kang</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Vives</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Vaccaro</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The halo vest: principles of application and management of complications</article-title><source>J Spinal Cord Med</source><year>2003</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>186</fpage><lpage>192</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14997956</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lieberman</surname><given-names>IH</given-names></name><name><surname>Webb</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cervical spine injuries in the elderly</article-title><source>J Bone Joint Surg Br</source><year>1994</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>877</fpage><lpage>881</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7983110</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>